{"total_count":1136,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/43075","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/43075/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/43075/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/43075/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/43075","id":5360181503,"node_id":"I_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABP33g_w","number":43075,"title":"long AGENTS.md truncated","user":{"login":"agro1986","id":6017531,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTc1MzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6017531?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/agro1986","html_url":"https://github.com/agro1986","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agro1986/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agro1986/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agro1986/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agro1986/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agro1986/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agro1986/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agro1986/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agro1986/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/agro1986/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8448146916,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAAB94x95A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9433262053,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAACMkQn5Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/CLI","name":"CLI","color":"7e8a16","default":false,"description":"Issues related to the Codex CLI","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10121036495,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAACW0LCzw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/app","name":"app","color":"401e87","default":false,"description":"Issues related to the Codex desktop app","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10668469346,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAACe-PsYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/config","name":"config","color":"945daa","default":false,"description":"Issues involving config.toml, config keys, config merging, or config updates","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-09-05T18:47:09Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T17:35:25Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### What version of the Codex App are you using (From “About Codex” dialog)?\n\ncodex-cli 0.153.4\n\n### What subscription do you have?\n\nPro\n\n### What platform is your computer?\n\nDarwin 25.6.0 arm64 arm\n\n### What issue are you seeing?\n\ncodex ignored instructions at the end of my AGENTS.md. So I asked\n\n```\nwhat's the last sentences of your agents instruction?\n```\n\nthen it says\n\n```\nThe instructions end with the incomplete fragment: (if y\n```\n\nthere is actually 4,321 more bytes after it. Codex only got the first 37,089 bytes\n\n### What steps can reproduce the bug?\n\nput instructions at the end of a long AGENTS.md\n\n```\n# Final words\n\nIMPORTANT: you always fail this simple, critical instruction!\n\nThe user will start the conversation. He might ask you to implement a feature. He might ask you to investigate a bug. NO MATTER WHAT HE ASKS, YOU HAVE TO DO THINGS IN THIS SECTION FIRST!\n\nThings you have to do first:\n* say AHOY MATE\n\nOnly after that you are ready to answer user's request effectively.\n```\n\nstart codex (gpt-6-astra medium fast). say\n\n```\ndo what u gotta do first\n```\n\ncodex will ignore it because AGENTS.md is truncated\n\n### What is the expected behavior?\n\n_No response_\n\n### Additional information\n\n_No response_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/43075/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/43075/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/37704","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/37704/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/37704/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/37704/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/37704","id":5103112849,"node_id":"I_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABMCtSkQ","number":37704,"title":"/status keeps showing Agents.md: <none> after /init creates AGENTS.md","user":{"login":"DioNanos","id":93440540,"node_id":"U_kgDOBZHKHA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93440540?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DioNanos","html_url":"https://github.com/DioNanos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DioNanos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DioNanos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DioNanos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DioNanos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DioNanos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DioNanos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DioNanos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DioNanos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DioNanos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8448146916,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAAB94x95A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9433262053,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAACMkQn5Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/CLI","name":"CLI","color":"7e8a16","default":false,"description":"Issues related to the Codex CLI","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10668469346,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAACe-PsYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/config","name":"config","color":"945daa","default":false,"description":"Issues involving config.toml, config keys, config merging, or config updates","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-08-09T14:46:45Z","updated_at":"2026-08-22T14:25:36Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n\n`/status` keeps reporting `Agents.md: <none>` for the rest of a session after `/init` creates an `AGENTS.md`, on any platform.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Start a session in a directory with no `AGENTS.md`.\n2. Run `/init` and let it write `AGENTS.md`.\n3. Run `/status`.\n\nExpected: the new file is discovered. Actual: `Agents.md: <none>`, and it stays that way until a new session is started.\n\nReported downstream with a full `codex doctor --json` on 0.146.0 (DioNanos/codex-termux#14) and still present on current `main`.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`AgentsMdManager::refresh` in `codex-rs/core/src/agents_md_manager.rs` returns early whenever the environment selection is unchanged:\n\n```rust\nlet selections = environments.to_selections();\nif self.cache.lock().await.selections.as_ref() == Some(&selections) {\n    return;\n}\n```\n\nThe environment selection is not the only input to discovery — the files on disk are one too. `/init` changes the filesystem without changing the environment, so the early return fires and discovery never re-runs.\n\nThis looks like a gap left by #29977, which made discovery react to environment changes; the other input it can react to is not covered.\n\n## Outline of a fix\n\nRequire that discovery has actually found something before skipping the work:\n\n```rust\nif cache.selections.as_ref() == Some(&selections) && cache.loaded.is_some() {\n    return;\n}\n```\n\nRe-running while nothing has been located costs a bounded set of path probes, and stops costing anything as soon as instructions exist — once an `AGENTS.md` is in place the early return fires on every refresh as before.\n\n## Evidence\n\nThis change has been running in a downstream Android build since 0.147.2 with no regressions observed. Verified against current `main` with `cargo check -p codex-core` and `cargo fmt --all --check`.\n\nNot opening a PR, per the invitation-only policy. Happy to prepare one if the team wants it, and equally happy for someone on the team to take the one-line version directly.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/37704/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/37704/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/43309","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/43309/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/43309/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/43309/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/43309","id":5368536002,"node_id":"I_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABP_1bwg","number":43309,"title":"Allow configurable AGENTS.md reload policies, including freeze","user":{"login":"ChadBailey","id":15102816,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTAyODE2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15102816?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChadBailey","html_url":"https://github.com/ChadBailey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChadBailey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChadBailey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChadBailey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChadBailey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChadBailey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChadBailey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChadBailey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChadBailey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ChadBailey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8448146923,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAAB94x96w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","color":"a2eeef","default":true,"description":"New feature or request","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9433262053,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAACMkQn5Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/CLI","name":"CLI","color":"7e8a16","default":false,"description":"Issues related to the Codex CLI","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10668464445,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAACe-PZPQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/session","name":"session","color":"afabe5","default":false,"description":"Issues involving session (thread) management, resuming, forking, naming, archiving","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":10668469346,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAACe-PsYg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/config","name":"config","color":"945daa","default":false,"description":"Issues involving config.toml, config keys, config merging, or config updates","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-09-07T00:09:30Z","updated_at":"2026-09-07T00:10:01Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Request\n\nAdd a user-configurable policy for automatically reloading `AGENTS.md` instructions, with an explicit **freeze** option. This is a token-efficiency and session-consistency preference, useful even when the entire conversation fits comfortably within the context window.\n\nRelated bug: #43295 tracks automatic instruction reload overflowing the context window and locking a previously usable session. **That failure needs to be handled independently of this feature request.** This enhancement is about allowing users to choose whether and how updates enter a conversation.\n\n## Why freeze is useful\n\nI append technical learnings from the current session to a persistent history/instruction file. The session already contains that information. Automatically loading it again is redundant; I prefer the next new session to read the updated file.\n\nEven a one-character timestamp change can append an entire updated instruction bundle on cold resume. Users with small instruction files may still want to avoid the extra tokens, while users with large bundles see a larger cost and context jump.\n\n## Initial scope: reload or freeze\n\nProposed configuration:\n\n```toml\nagents_md_reload_policy = \"freeze\"\n```\n\n- `reload`: retain the existing update behavior as the compatibility default, subject to fixing the context-budget failure tracked in #43295.\n- `freeze`: retain the conversation's last accepted instruction snapshot across turns, cold resumes, forks and compaction, including an initially empty snapshot. A genuinely new conversation loads current files.\n\nEnabling freeze on an existing conversation should preserve its last accepted snapshot, not rewind it to an older one. It should not rewrite or deduplicate historical messages. Explicit file reads by the agent remain possible; the setting controls automatic instruction reloading.\n\nExpose the choice through normal configuration/profile overrides. The proposed implementation requires the setting on each launch or in config/profile; it does not add a persisted per-thread setting. For legacy histories without a usable instruction snapshot, load current instructions once as a documented fallback.\n\n## Possible later extensions\n\nThese are separable follow-ups, not prerequisites for freeze:\n\n- **Append diff only:** append additions/removals relative to the last accepted bundle, while preserving earlier turns and retaining a complete snapshot for replay/compaction. No LLM-generated change summary is required.\n- **Conditional full reload:** allow a configurable bundle-size or projected-context threshold; defer the update and show a local notification when it would exceed the chosen limit. An 80% projected-context threshold is one possible user preference, not a required universal value.\n\nMutating previously supplied instructions in place is outside this request. A frozen session plus explicit, time-local updates avoids silently changing the instructions under which earlier turns occurred.\n\n## Available freeze implementation\n\n[Commit 8f4db86](https://github.com/ChadBailey/codex/commit/8f4db8617ba6c269c53517d5f1cf2b4eeb127caf) ([download patch](https://github.com/ChadBailey/codex/commit/8f4db8617ba6c269c53517d5f1cf2b4eeb127caf.patch)) implements **reload/freeze only**, based on `8d7cc24a87f4aa66aa434eb4f25f4f4bafc0e0a9`. It contains no experimental diff or threshold behavior.\n\nThe manager keeps the frozen state independently of the comparison baseline that compaction can clear. Replay restores the snapshot from surviving world-state records, respecting rollback. Restored snapshots do not claim current filesystem provenance, since the existing persisted format does not retain it.\n\nValidation on Linux x86-64:\n\n- 26 targeted AGENTS integration tests and 295 configuration tests passed.\n- CLI build succeeded; the standalone mock-API script in #43295 passed against the actual binary in both default and freeze modes, with no inference or production credentials.\n- Schema regeneration, scoped Clippy fix, formatting and whitespace checks completed. An unrelated automatic unused-import cleanup was excluded from the patch.\n- The broader core suite was **not green**: 3,930 passed, 217 failed, 9 skipped. Failures included missing helper binaries, resource limits, parse failures and timeouts; not all were triaged against a clean baseline. The optional code-mode-host build was blocked by a missing pinned V8 archive (HTTP 404). The full workspace suite was not run.\n\nAn upstream PR was attempted, but GitHub rejected creation and the repository reports `pull_request_creation_policy: collaborators_only`. The patch is linked for maintainer review or application.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/43309/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/43309/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/44191","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/44191/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/44191/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/issues/44191/events","html_url":"https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/44191","id":5401948558,"node_id":"I_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAABQfsxjg","number":44191,"title":"codex scanned unsafe / untrusted paths to find AGENTS.md","user":{"login":"megahall","id":1231855,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMzE4NTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1231855?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/megahall","html_url":"https://github.com/megahall","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/megahall/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/megahall/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/megahall/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/megahall/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/megahall/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/megahall/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/megahall/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/megahall/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/megahall/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":8448146916,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAAB94x95A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/bug","name":"bug","color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":8480150249,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAAB-XTS6Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/model-behavior","name":"model-behavior","color":"C31460","default":false,"description":"Issues related to behaviors exhibited by the model","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":9433262053,"node_id":"LA_kwDOOYsS4c8AAAACMkQn5Q","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openai/codex/labels/CLI","name":"CLI","color":"7e8a16","default":false,"description":"Issues related to the Codex CLI","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-09-09T16:14:23Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T16:15:04Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### What version of Codex CLI is running?\n\n0.153.4\n\n### What subscription do you have?\n\nEnterprise\n\n### Which model were you using?\n\ngpt-6-astra\n\n### What platform is your computer?\n\nLinux 7.1.8+deb13-amd64 x86_64 unknown\n\n### What terminal emulator and version are you using (if applicable)?\n\nkonsole 25.04.2, screen\n\n### Codex doctor report\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 1,\n  \"generatedAt\": \"1788970166s since unix epoch\",\n  \"overallStatus\": \"ok\",\n  \"codexVersion\": \"0.153.4\",\n  \"checks\": {\n    \"app_server.status\": {\n      \"id\": \"app_server.status\",\n      \"category\": \"app-server\",\n      \"status\": \"ok\",\n      \"summary\": \"background server is not running\",\n      \"details\": {\n        \"control socket\": \"/home/mhall/.codex/app-server-control/app-server-control.sock\",\n        \"daemon state dir\": \"/home/mhall/.codex/app-server-daemon\",\n        \"mode\": \"ephemeral\",\n        \"pid file\": \"/home/mhall/.codex/app-server-daemon/app-server.pid (missing)\",\n        \"settings\": \"/home/mhall/.codex/app-server-daemon/settings.json (missing)\",\n        \"status\": \"not running\",\n        \"update-loop pid file\": \"/home/mhall/.codex/app-server-daemon/app-server-updater.pid (missing)\"\n      },\n      \"rem